        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ٹانگ (ṭāng) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from ṭaṅga, \"leg\" (CDIAL 5428). CDIAL lists it under ṭaṅka, which the old lexicons gloss both \"rod, spike\" and \"leg\", and asks whether the word first meant \"stick\"."
            }
          ]
        },
